// #2905, and the third time this family shipped: #1460 (`Console::write_char`,
// `Console::write_err_char`), #2903 (`sleep_blocking`), #2905
// (`Console::read_char`). A builtin name mapped onto a CONDITIONALLY reserved
// host import, without a reservation of its own, falls back to a stub of
// another arity -- so the program compiles clean, writes a `.wasm`, reports
// success, and emits a module wasmtime refuses to validate. Each fix was
// "remember to add the name in the other place", which is exactly the step
// that keeps being missed. Reads the two sources, so it needs no generation.
